From a984a43785eae77e976fad40cb5e7895ea5507fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dreamstone Ruination <claude@example.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 03:28:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Blue Moon Teddiursa line v10 Bloodsnow palette (Dreamstone
 Ruination starters)

Replaces the canonical normal palettes for the Teddiursa evolution line with
the Cormorian Bloodsnow identity: snow-white fur with blood-red lunar
markings. This is the second of three starter palette sets for the project
(Frigibax already shipped; Tinkatink line to follow).

Per the project bible, all three starter options are permanently 'shiny'
from selection (the form players see is always the Cormorian palette), so
these changes go in normal.pal/overworld_normal.pal rather than shiny.pal.

Files modified per species:
  graphics/pokemon/teddiursa/{normal.pal, overworld_normal.pal}
  graphics/pokemon/teddiursa/{anim_front.png, back.png, overworld.png}
  graphics/pokemon/ursaring/{normal.pal, overworld_normal.pal}
  graphics/pokemon/ursaring/{anim_front.png, anim_frontf.png}
  graphics/pokemon/ursaring/{back.png, backf.png}
  graphics/pokemon/ursaring/{overworld.png, overworldf.png}
  graphics/pokemon/ursaluna/bloodmoon/{normal.pal, overworld_normal.pal}
  graphics/pokemon/ursaluna/bloodmoon/{front.png, back.png, overworld.png}

Approach (per DREAMSTONE_HANDOFF.md):
- Per-index sprite analysis followed by per-pixel reassignment where the
  canonical artist used a single palette index for multiple body parts
  (e.g. Ursaring's idx 8/11 yellow shared between chest ring and chest fluff)
- Front and overworld palettes analyzed independently (different index
  meanings between battle sprite and overworld sprite)
- Female Ursaring variants (anim_frontf.png, backf.png, overworldf.png)
  processed with the same transformation as male variants
- All RGB values are GBA-safe multiples of 8 for accurate
  preview-to-render fidelity

Per-species design notes:

Teddiursa (Blue Moon):
- Snow-white body fur (canonical orange family idx 1,2,3,4,7 -> white)
- Canonical cream muzzle patch preserved (idx 9 unchanged)
- Forehead crescent: canonical white -> blood red (idx 6)

Ursaring (Blue Moon):
- Snow-white body fur (canonical brown family idx 1,2,3,6,12 -> white)
- Per-pixel separation: chest RING pixels (lower body) kept at idx 8/11
  -> blood red; non-ring 'yellow' pixels (chest fluff, face mask)
  relocated to canonical cream/tan
- Per-pixel separation: idx 12 face cluster (lower lip/chin) kept at
  canonical tan; idx 12 body pixels relocated to white
- Per-pixel: 4-pixel snout-edge cluster at (22,7), (22,8), (22,9), (23,6)
  preserved as canonical brown via repurposed idx 10
- Canonical mouth (idx 13) preserved

Bloodmoon Ursaluna (Blue Moon):
- Canonical browns preserved with chocolate-aggressive shift (+22R, -10G,
  -15B) for slightly richer chocolate tone
- Canonical gray fur (idx 2,3,6,12) -> snow white via dominant remap
- Green eye (idx 9) -> blood red
- Pink moon markings (idx 7, 11) -> unified blood red
- Gold collar (idx 10) -> chocolate brown (with aggressive shift)
- Overworld browns match front sprite chocolate values directly

Color identity (all values multiples of 8):
- Blood red bright: (224, 48, 64) - all forehead/chest markings, eyes
- Blood red dark:   (160, 32, 48) - shadow/dark variant of markings
- Snow white:       (248, 248, 248) - main body fur

Verification:
1. Apply patch in source tree
2. Make rule '%.gbapal: %.pal' will rebuild compiled artifacts
3. Compile
4. Players selecting the Teddiursa starter line will see the Cormorian
   Bloodsnow identity throughout battle (front/back) and overworld
   (follower) sprites
